{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917309639},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to:\n1. Find the total number of farmers markets in the US from a dataset\n2. Get census data for US population\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents to 4 decimal places\n4. Use tools to do the math and verify everything\n\nAccording to the project instructions, I should:\n1. First check `xorq_semantic_models` to see if there's an existing semantic model\n2. Then `xorq_catalog_list_aliases` to see existing aliases\n3. Only if needed, ingest the sources using build scripts\n4. Use `xorq_select` to get values\n5. Use `xorq_verify` to verify all numbers\n6. Never state a number I didn't get from `xorq_select`\n\nLet me start by checking what's already in the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking the xorq catalog for existing data."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_015NZtxsvLSZADcV3j7FPbQh","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01R1p1BrJNunGVk1dNV9eTrH","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":342,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8306,"totalTokens":8658,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.00171